Subject: [PATCH 02/34] flashnext: two-rank KV formats, indexer window,
 prompt-cache snapshots with drafts, recipe ports

The two-rank foundation the rest of the series builds on:
- MXFP8 dense layers cut by head at --tp 2, and --kv-cache fp8, nvfp4 and fp8k_nvfp4v at one and two ranks
  (quantized caches are chosen with --kv-cache; bf16 stays the default).
- A window of raw indexer keys per stream at --tp 2 (design: docs/flashnext-tp2-indexer-split.md).
- Prompt-cache snapshots with MTP drafts at --tp 2, which upstream refused (design: docs/flashnext-tp2-snapshots.md).
- Ports of patches 0001-0017 of MiaAI-Lab's Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-Single-DGX-Spark-TensorFold recipe (MIT; "single-Spark
  recipe" below, each change names its recipe patch): vision tower, image budget, --kv-cache fp8, fp8 reader prefetch,
  prefill speed, sampled draws, n-gram gather, host draws, HC read-out, two-stage prompt tile, draft stop rule,
  adapted to the head split.
- Our own, not from the recipe: NVFP4 KV caches, YaRN past the trained window, the shared pool with its memory
  ledger, and /health live rates.

Changes, in the order they were made:
- docs(flashnext): design for prompt-cache snapshots with MTP drafts at --tp 2
- feat(vision): load NVIDIA's quantized vision tower (single-Spark recipe 0001)
- feat(vision): a request's image budget up to 16,384 tokens (single-Spark recipe 0002)
- build(cuda): run the Flash Next, native and CUDA runtime modules' host tests alone
- feat(flashnext): cut MXFP8 dense layers by head at --tp 2 (FP4-Local)
- feat(flashnext): prompt-cache snapshots with MTP drafts at --tp 2
- test(flashnext): host tests for two-rank snapshot frames, agreement and failure paths
- feat(flashnext-cuda): --kv-cache fp8 (single-Spark recipe 0003)
- feat(flashnext): port --kv-cache fp8 onto the head split
- feat(flashnext-cuda): fp8 reader prefetch, bf16 head cache, 4-bit draft head (single-Spark recipe 0005)
- feat(flashnext-cuda): prefill speed at one rank (single-Spark recipe 0006, adapted)
- feat(flashnext): port NVFP4 KV, --kv-cache nvfp4 and fp8k_nvfp4v
- feat(flashnext-cuda): sampled draws from GPU top-k candidates (single-Spark recipe 0008)
- feat(flashnext-cuda): one n-gram gather for all of a shared pass's streams (single-Spark recipe 0010, adapted)
- feat(flashnext): quantized KV caches at --tp 2 (two-rank NVFP4)
- feat(flashnext-cuda): host draws on worker threads, faster candidate kernel (single-Spark recipe 0011)
- feat(flashnext-cuda): fused native HC read-out, shared output in place, head pieces (single-Spark recipe 0014,
  adapted)
- feat(qmmf): two-stage MX128 prompt tile, two blocks an SM, behind TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_GEMM2 (single-Spark recipe
  0015)
- feat(flashnext-cuda): running-product draft stop rule, per-draft floor past TF_FLASHNEXT_PRODUCT_STREAMS
  (single-Spark recipe 0017, adapted)
- feat(flashnext-cuda): NVFP4 KV caches, --kv-cache nvfp4 and fp8k_nvfp4v
- feat(flashnext-cuda): YaRN past the trained window, TF_FLASHNEXT_YARN
- docs(flashnext): design for the indexer keys at --tp 2 without a whole copy a rank
- feat(flashnext): a window of raw indexer keys a stream at --tp 2
- test(flashnext): host reference for splitting pooled indexer blocks by position
- test(flashnext): the rank snapshot fake engine sets the KV format and index window
- feat(flashnext-cuda): streams and the prompt cache share one pool, with a memory floor and ledger
- feat(server): reserve image preparation in the memory ledger before decoding
- fix(picture): one PNG header, and compressed text inflated into one bounded buffer
- fix(server): image preparation's wait for memory ends when the client goes
- fix(flashnext): batched attention takes bf16 caches only; a quantized main or draft-head cache goes lane by lane
- feat(server): /health live rates over 10 s and the engine's totals on /health and /metrics
- test(flashnext): the two-rank GPU snapshot tests pass no draft to Session.save and restore
- fix(native): NVFP4 and fp8k_nvfp4v caches refuse --learn-conversations and --spill-gib at startup like fp8

Flags this patch adds (a flag's default is its unset value; unset leaves the engine as it was
before the flag, and a knob named under another flag only matters when that flag is on):
- TENSORFOLD_MEMORY_FLOOR_GIB=<GiB> (with TF_FLASHNEXT_SHARED_POOL; 0 to 4096, 0: no floor): the free memory the
  shared pool keeps; unset: the reserve, up to 10 GiB.
- TENSORFOLD_MEMORY_HEADROOM_MIB=<MiB> (with TF_FLASHNEXT_SHARED_POOL): room above the memory floor for host
  transients no decision prices; load refuses a bad value.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_GATHER_EARLY=1: a shared pass gathers every stream's n-gram rows in one pool call (not one call a
  stream).
- TF_FLASHNEXT_GATHER_LOG=1: what a shared pass waits for the n-gram gather at the PLE layer.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_HC2_DN / TF_FLASHNEXT_HC2_UP: the CTA row tile (16 * N rows) of those two kernels.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_HC2_MIN: the fewest rows of a prompt pass that take the fused read-out (default 768; its CTAs need rows
  to fill the GPU).
- TF_FLASHNEXT_HEAD_KV=fp8 (or =main) keeps the head's cache in the main format, nvfp4 and fp8k_nvfp4v too (whose bf16
  head costs 1,440 and 1,216 bytes more a position).
- TF_FLASHNEXT_HEAD_PIECE: the rows a prompt chunk's MTP head pass takes at most (default 256, the decode rounds'
  piece).
- TF_FLASHNEXT_HOST_DRAW_THREADS=N (0, the default: one thread, the plain scans and one download a row): N workers
  beside the engine thread, and each row's top_k found sixteen columns a compare (the same columns, in the same
  order).
- TF_FLASHNEXT_INDEX_WINDOW: unset or "1" keeps the window at --tp 2, "0" keeps a row a position.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_PRODUCT_STREAMS: added by the change "running-product draft stop rule, per-draft floor past
  TF_FLASHNEXT_PRODUCT_STREAMS (single-Spark recipe 0017, adapted)".
- TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_GEMM2=1: the prompt tile runs with two stages and two blocks an SM (same arithmetic, same bits).
- TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_HC2=1: the native hyper-connection read-out of prompt passes (TF_FLASHNEXT_HC2_MIN rows or more)
  runs on two fused kernels (flashnext_hcf.cu hcn: the norm formed in the down tile and in the up epilogue, the up
  rows mixed in place) instea...
- TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_MX128=N: MXFP8 projections of N columns or more take the relaxed 128 x 128 prompt tile in prompt
  passes (default 1024).
- TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_SHARED_DIRECT=1: a prompt pass's MoE write-back reads the shared expert's fp32 output in place
  instead of a copy of it in y's last slot (the same value in the same fused-multiply-add order; one launch and 62 MB
  per layer less).
- TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_SYNC=1: drain the stream after every non-final prompt chunk, as v1.1.4 did.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_SAMPLE_CAND=1: a sampled draw (a verify window's rows, the draft head's row) reads its row's top_k best
  scores and columns, selected on the device (fn_row_cand), instead of the whole row copied to the host and scanned.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_SHARED_POOL=1 (one rank) charges each stream only its fixed part at startup (about 0.32 GiB with the
  MTP head and vision), so the prompt cache gets its --prompt-cache-gib beside them.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_YARN=4 (one rank) serves --context past the trained window, up to 4 x 262,144: Qwen's YaRN recipe
  (rope_type yarn, factor 4, the ramp over pairs 14 to 22), with the attention factor 0.1 ln 4 + 1 folded into the
  rotated norms' gammas as the Pyth...
- TF_FLASHNEXT_YARN_RAMP_POSITIONS (with TF_FLASHNEXT_YARN): moves the YaRN ramp (as vLLM's M-RoPE does); unset: the
  default ramp.
